# LSP Server Capabilities

File: ooda/lsp/docs/CAPABILITIES.oot

The openOODA native LSP engine advertises a fixed, minimal set of
capabilities in the `initialize` response. This doc is the
authoritative spec for that declaration. The single source of truth
in the source tree is `ooda/lsp/server/lsp_server_capabilities.oo`,
which returns one constant JSON string. The doc duplicates that
string, explains every entry, and lists what is intentionally
NOT advertised and why.

## 1. The capability JSON

The `initialize` response body is:

```json
{
  "capabilities": {
    "textDocumentSync": {
      "openClose": true,
      "change": 1
    },
    "completionProvider": {
      "resolveProvider": true,
      "triggerCharacters": [".", "&", ":"]
    },
    "hoverProvider": true,
    "definitionProvider": true,
    "documentSymbolProvider": true,
    "documentFormattingProvider": true,
    "codeActionProvider": true,
    "documentLinkProvider": {
      "resolveProvider": false
    },
    "inlayHintProvider": true,
    "diagnosticProvider": {
      "interFileDependencies": false,
      "workspaceDiagnostics": false
    },
    "executeCommandProvider": {
      "commands": [
        "ooda.lsp.version",
        "ooda.lsp.indexSize",
        "ooda.lsp.echo"
      ]
    },
    "workspace": {
      "workspaceFolders": {
        "supported": true
      }
    }
  }
}
```

`serverInfo` is set to `{ "name": "openooda-lsp", "version": "0.5.0" }`
where `0.5.0` comes from the `lsp=` line in `VERSION`. The engine
version returned by `ooda.lsp.version` is a separate value
(`lsp_facade_version()` in `lsp_version.oo`) and is the
double-run-proof SSoT.

## 2. Capability-by-capability rationale

### 2.1 `textDocumentSync` (kind: full, change: 1)

- `openClose: true` — the server wants `didOpen` so it can compute
  the governance diagnostics and emit `publishDiagnostics`.
- `change: 1` — full sync. The client sends the full text on every
  `didChange`. The server does not implement incremental sync (LSP
  3.17 `change: 2`).
- **Note**: `textDocument/didClose` is NOT in the dispatcher
  (lsp_server_dispatch.oo). The `openClose: true` flag is therefore
  over-advertised today. A `didClose` will be rejected with
  `-32601 Method not found`. The 0.5.0 server expects the client to
  ignore this and not surface it as an error.

### 2.2 `completionProvider` (resolveProvider: true, trigger: . & :)

- `triggerCharacters` are `.`, `&`, `:`. `.` is the namespace
  member access, `&` is the OCap capability token, `:` is the type
  annotation.
- `resolveProvider: true` advertises that the server accepts
  `completionItem/resolve` to fill in `documentation`. The 0.5.0
  server returns the static detail on the initial call and does not
  distinguish a resolve pass; the flag is honest but minimal.

### 2.3 `hoverProvider: true`

- Hover returns a markdown Contents block: the Academy 4-element
  header (Title, Logline, Setup, Beats) parsed from the source text
  prepended to the canonical symbol's signature and doc. `null` for
  unknown symbols.

### 2.4 `definitionProvider: true`

- Definition returns a `Location` for capability builtins (URI is
  `ooda/runtime/chs_rt_*.c`) and for user `pub fn` (URI + line + col
  from the compiler index). `null` otherwise.

### 2.5 `documentSymbolProvider: true`

- DocumentSymbol returns `kind=12` (Function) entries extracted by a
  `pub fn ` scan. No class, interface, or namespace kinds. No
  hierarchical nesting. The server is single-file today and does not
  model the module tree.

### 2.6 `documentFormattingProvider: true`

- Formatting returns a single full-file `TextEdit` with normalized
  indentation: tabs to 4 spaces, trailing whitespace trimmed. The
  formatter is a single pass; it does not implement an LSP
  `DocumentRangeFormattingProvider` and does not honor
  `DocumentFormattingOptions`.

### 2.7 `codeActionProvider: true`

- CodeAction returns up to 4 fixes keyed off the diagnostic code:
  `E_CAP`, `E_PARSE`, `E_EM_WEIGHT`, `E_CAP_ATTENUATE`. The server
  does not advertise a `codeActionKinds` array; all actions are of
  kind `quickfix`.

### 2.8 `documentLinkProvider` (resolveProvider: false)

- DocumentLink scans for `&Cap` references and resolves each to an
  oodac/ runtime source URI. The server does not implement
  `documentLink/resolve`; the targets are returned directly. Hence
  `resolveProvider: false`.

### 2.9 `inlayHintProvider: true`

- InlayHint scans for `let x = <literal>` and emits a hint with the
  inferred literal type: `String`, `Int`, `Bool`. The hint is emitted
  with `kind: 1` (Type). The server does not honor
  `InlayHintOptions.resolveProvider`.

### 2.10 `diagnosticProvider` (interFileDependencies: false, workspaceDiagnostics: false)

- Pull mode (LSP 3.16+) is supported via `textDocument/diagnostic`.
  The response is `{ items: [...] }` synchronous.
- `interFileDependencies: false` because the 6 governance
  diagnostics are local to the single file.
- `workspaceDiagnostics: false` because there is no
  `workspace/diagnostic` handler in the dispatcher.

### 2.11 `executeCommandProvider`

- 3 commands: `ooda.lsp.version`, `ooda.lsp.indexSize`,
  `ooda.lsp.echo`. See `protocol.oot` §7.1 for request and response
  shapes.

### 2.12 `workspace.workspaceFolders.supported: true`

- The server uses a single root from `initialize.params.rootUri`. The
  `workspaceFolders` capability is advertised for clients that
  require the flag, but the server does not implement
  `workspace/workspaceFolders` or `workspace/didChangeWorkspaceFolders`.

## 3. What is NOT supported

The following standard LSP 3.17 methods are intentionally NOT
advertised. Each entry has a one-line rationale.

| Method | Status | Rationale |
|--------|--------|-----------|
| `workspace/didChangeWatchedFiles` | Not advertised | The stdlib index is rescanned at startup. Slice D removed the no-op handler and the capability lie. |
| `workspace/symbol` | Not advertised | No workspace-wide search; the index is file-scoped. |
| `workspace/diagnostic` | Not advertised | Governance diagnostics are file-local (`interFileDependencies: false`). |
| `textDocument/didClose` | Dispatcher missing | Over-advertised via `textDocumentSync.openClose`; clients should ignore the mismatch. |
| `textDocument/references` | Not advertised | No cross-file reference index; the compiler index is single-file. |
| `textDocument/rename` | Not advertised | No rename-aware symbol table; refactor is out of scope. |
| `textDocument/signatureHelp` | Not advertised | The `.oo` syntax does not need paren-completion; cap + type sigs are inline. |
| `textDocument/rangeFormatting` | Not advertised | The formatter is full-file only. |
| `textDocument/onTypeFormatting` | Not advertised | Trigger characters already drive completion. |
| `textDocument/documentHighlight` | Not advertised | No semantics for "this binding is used here". |
| `textDocument/foldingRange` | Not advertised | Editor-side. |
| `textDocument/selectionRange` | Not advertised | Editor-side. |
| `textDocument/semanticTokens` | Not advertised | The 6 governance diagnostics are not token streams. |
| `textDocument/moniker` | Not advertised | No module name resolution; `ANCHOR.oo` paths are the closest equivalent and are not exposed over LSP. |
| `textDocument/typeDefinition` | Not advertised | `pub fn` is the only top-level decl with a definition URI; types do not have one. |
| `textDocument/implementation` | Not advertised | No interfaces in `.oo`. |
| `textDocument/prepareTypeHierarchy` | Not advertised | No type hierarchy. |
| `textDocument/colorProvider` | Not advertised | No semantic color values. |
| `textDocument/prepareCallHierarchy` | Not advertised | The call graph is not built. |

## 4. SSoT: where the JSON lives

The capability JSON is one constant string in
`ooda/lsp/server/lsp_server_capabilities.oo`. It is not assembled
from per-capability fields; any change to a capability's shape
must be made in that file. The `lsp_server_handle_initialize` in
`lsp_server_handlers.oo` reads the constant and frames the
`initialize` response.

The `version` in `serverInfo` is the `lsp=` line in `VERSION`. The
`ooda.lsp.version` executeCommand result is the
`lsp_facade_version()` constant in `lsp_version.oo`. The two
versions are intentionally separate: `serverInfo.version` is the
package version (driven by the release script), `ooda.lsp.version`
is the engine version (driven by the double-run proof).
